# Lesson 2, new hand: two five-card suits, open the higher.
title: Two five-card suits
id: L02-22
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.2, 2.6
student: S
board: 22
dealer: E
vulnerable: EW

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  K63    K963   A54    Q83
  E  J982   T5     JT872  A6
  S  7      AQJ84  K3     KJ952
  W  AQT54  72     Q96    T74

auction:
  E Pass
  S 1H*    = 13+ points, at least four hearts
     key: 14 HCP, plus 2 for the singleton and 1 for the doubleton: 17. With two five-card suits, open the higher-ranking.
     not 1C: With two five-card suits, which one did the lesson say to open first?
     not 2H: A two-bid needs 22+. Did you count 17?
     not *: With two five-card suits, open the higher-ranking one.
  W Pass
  N 3H     = an opening hand or better and four hearts: forcing to game
  E Pass
  S 4H*    = Game
     key: Partner showed an opening hand or better and four hearts. Your side has well over 25 and nine hearts. Bid game.
     not Pass: 3♥ shows an opening hand or better. With your 17, is there enough for game?
     not 3NT: You have nine hearts between you. Which game is the better bet?
     not 4C: We won't worry about slams yet. Partner showed enough for game: bid it.
  W Pass
  N Pass
  E Pass

auction recap:
  With two five-card suits you open the higher one, 1♥. Partner's jump to
  3♥ showed an opening hand or better and four hearts. Your side has about 30 points
  and a nine-card fit, so you bid game. You are declarer, because you bid
  hearts first, and so West will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  trumps out: 4
  remind: What is the contract? How many tricks do you need?

play:
  1   W H7  N HK  E HT  S H4
      note: Win with dummy's ♥K, the high card from the short side, so that you can draw the next round from your hand.
  2   N H3  E H5  S HA  W H2
      note: The plan: draw trumps, then set up your clubs. This round draws the opponents' last trump.
  3   S C2  W C4  N CQ  E CA
      note: Now drive out the ♣A.
  4   E DJ  S D3  W D6  N DA
  5   N C3  E C6  S CJ  W C7
      note: Back to your clubs.
  6   S CK  W CT  N C8  E D2
      note: Your clubs are winners now.
  7   S C9  W S4  N S3  E S2
      note: Keep going.
  8   S C5  W S5  N S6  E D7
      note: The last club.
  9   S DK  W D9  N D4  E D8
      note: The ♦K.
  10  S S7  W SA  N SK  E S8
      note: Give up the ♠A.
  11  W ST  N H9  E S9  S H8
      note: Dummy trumps with the ♥9.
  12  N H6  E DT  S HJ  W DQ
      note: Dummy's last trump. Your ♥J wins, since nobody else has a trump.
  13  S HQ  W SQ  N D5  E SJ
      note: Your last trump. 11 tricks: 4♥ made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  The plan: draw trumps, then set up and run your clubs.

  4♥ made with an overtrick. Opening the higher of your two five-card
  suits let partner show her heart support right away.
